WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.977
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Cambodia Grade twelve English.

2
00:00:06.277 --> 00:00:09.826
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:10.126 --> 00:00:16.436
Unit eight: Gerunds and Infinitives. Today you will choose -ing or to + verb after common verbs.

4
00:00:16.736 --> 00:00:19.411
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.367 --> 00:00:23.274
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.117 --> 00:00:24.990
Gerund.

7
00:00:25.983 --> 00:00:28.308
Gerund means a verb used as a noun with -ing.

8
00:00:28.917 --> 00:00:30.208
Swimming is fun.

9
00:00:30.817 --> 00:00:33.074
Your turn. Say: Gerund.

10
00:00:35.933 --> 00:00:36.923
Gerund.

11
00:00:37.683 --> 00:00:38.777
Infinitive.

12
00:00:39.783 --> 00:00:42.154
Infinitive means to + base verb.

13
00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:43.995
I want to learn.

14
00:00:44.583 --> 00:00:47.828
Your turn. Say: Infinitive.

15
00:00:50.667 --> 00:00:51.714
Infinitive.

16
00:00:52.450 --> 00:00:53.358
Enjoy.

17
00:00:54.350 --> 00:00:56.013
Enjoy means to like doing.

18
00:00:56.617 --> 00:00:57.780
I enjoy reading.

19
00:00:58.383 --> 00:01:01.314
Your turn. Say: Enjoy.

20
00:01:04.167 --> 00:01:05.075
Enjoy.

21
00:01:05.817 --> 00:01:06.783
Avoid.

22
00:01:07.783 --> 00:01:09.725
Avoid means to stay away from.

23
00:01:10.317 --> 00:01:11.805
Avoid making noise.

24
00:01:12.417 --> 00:01:15.290
Your turn. Say: Avoid.

25
00:01:18.133 --> 00:01:18.972
Avoid.

26
00:01:19.717 --> 00:01:20.602
Decide.

27
00:01:21.617 --> 00:01:23.535
Decide means to make a choice.

28
00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:25.674
I decided to study.

29
00:01:26.283 --> 00:01:29.307
Your turn. Say: Decide.

30
00:01:32.167 --> 00:01:33.191
Decide.

31
00:01:33.950 --> 00:01:34.939
Manage.

32
00:01:35.950 --> 00:01:38.147
Manage means to succeed in doing.

33
00:01:38.750 --> 00:01:40.378
She managed to finish.

34
00:01:40.983 --> 00:01:43.554
Your turn. Say: Manage.

35
00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:47.250
Manage.

36
00:01:48.017 --> 00:01:49.006
Remember.

37
00:01:50.017 --> 00:01:52.063
Remember means to keep in mind.

38
00:01:52.650 --> 00:01:54.069
Remember to call me.

39
00:01:54.683 --> 00:01:57.289
Your turn. Say: Remember.

40
00:02:00.133 --> 00:02:01.251
Remember.

41
00:02:02.017 --> 00:02:02.867
Stop.

42
00:02:03.883 --> 00:02:05.790
Stop means to end an action.

43
00:02:06.383 --> 00:02:07.663
He stopped talking.

44
00:02:08.250 --> 00:02:10.542
Your turn. Say: Stop.

45
00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:14.146
Stop.

46
00:02:14.933 --> 00:02:18.712
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:19.550 --> 00:02:21.886
Visal, which verbs take the gerund?

48
00:02:22.983 --> 00:02:32.692
Enjoy, avoid, finish, keep, suggest and mind are followed by -ing, such as I enjoy reading and She suggested going early.

49
00:02:33.783 --> 00:02:35.678
Which verbs take the infinitive?

50
00:02:36.783 --> 00:02:46.538
Want, decide, hope, plan, manage and refuse are followed by to + verb, such as I decided to study and We hope to win.

51
00:02:47.650 --> 00:02:49.104
Are there verbs with both?

52
00:02:50.217 --> 00:03:02.371
Yes, with different meanings. Remember to lock the door means do it. Remember locking it means recall that you did. Stop to eat means pause to eat, and stop eating means quit.

53
00:03:03.533 --> 00:03:05.498
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:06.350 --> 00:03:09.859
Grammar focus: verb plus -ing or to plus verb.

55
00:03:10.159 --> 00:03:11.404
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:12.117 --> 00:03:13.896
I enjoy reading in the evening.

57
00:03:14.783 --> 00:03:16.818
I decided to study medicine.

58
00:03:17.767 --> 00:03:25.019
Enjoy, avoid and finish take -ing. Want, decide and hope take to + verb. Remember and stop change meaning with the form.

59
00:03:25.783 --> 00:03:28.807
Be careful! Don't say: I enjoy to read.

60
00:03:30.767 --> 00:03:32.406
Say: I enjoy reading.

61
00:03:32.706 --> 00:03:34.149
Enjoy + -ing.

62
00:03:34.933 --> 00:03:37.980
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:38.767 --> 00:03:40.035
Plans for Study.

64
00:03:40.335 --> 00:03:42.265
Bopha enjoys reading in the evening.

65
00:03:43.267 --> 00:03:45.057
She decided to study medicine.

66
00:03:46.067 --> 00:03:48.275
She avoids wasting time on her phone.

67
00:03:49.267 --> 00:03:51.533
She managed to finish the book last week.

68
00:03:52.533 --> 00:03:54.463
She will remember to bring her notes.

69
00:03:55.567 --> 00:03:59.986
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:00.850 --> 00:04:02.664
Enjoy is followed by blank.

71
00:04:02.964 --> 00:04:06.942
A, to + verb. B, base verb. C, -ing.

72
00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:12.174
The answer is C: -ing.

73
00:04:13.317 --> 00:04:15.165
Decide is followed by blank.

74
00:04:15.465 --> 00:04:18.956
A, to + verb. B, -ing. C, that only.

75
00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:24.418
The answer is A: to + verb.

76
00:04:25.583 --> 00:04:27.536
Remember to lock means blank.

77
00:04:27.836 --> 00:04:31.014
A, never. B, do it. C, you did it.

78
00:04:34.567 --> 00:04:36.462
The answer is B: do it.

79
00:04:37.617 --> 00:04:39.059
Avoid blank noise.

80
00:04:39.359 --> 00:04:42.397
A, to make. B, make. C, making.

81
00:04:45.933 --> 00:04:47.875
The answer is C: making.

82
00:04:49.017 --> 00:04:50.610
Stop eating means blank.

83
00:04:50.910 --> 00:04:54.598
A, quit eating. B, pause to eat. C, start.

84
00:04:58.133 --> 00:05:00.121
The answer is A: quit eating.

85
00:05:01.333 --> 00:05:04.473
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:05.317 --> 00:05:06.678
What do you enjoy doing?

87
00:05:15.483 --> 00:05:17.111
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:17.411 --> 00:05:25.755
I enjoy reading English stories in the evening. I also like listening to songs. I have decided to speak English every day.

89
00:05:26.055 --> 00:05:27.881
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:28.783 --> 00:05:33.514
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and verb plus -ing or to plus verb.

91
00:05:33.814 --> 00:05:38.405
Today's value is dedication. Practise a little every day, and you will get better.

92
00:05:38.705 --> 00:05:41.125
See you in Unit nine. Goodbye!

93
00:05:41.425 --> 00:05:44.345
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

